2. The problem can be solved through multiple steps. First we need to figure out how many minutes Movie C was. Movie C was 1.25 hours equal to 1.25 * 60 = 75 minutes long. Next, using this information we can calculate how long Movie B was. Movie B was 5 minutes longer than movie C, so it was 75 + 5 = 80 minutes. Finally, we can calculate how long Movie A was. Movie A was one-fourth the length of Movie B, so it was 80 / 4 = 20 minutes.

